WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.565 --> 00:00:02.956
- When I'm not excited about something,

00:00:02.956 --> 00:00:05.173
then I want to give up
or I don't want to do it.

00:00:05.173 --> 00:00:06.758
I want to go back to
thinking about my dream.

00:00:06.758 --> 00:00:07.947
I've always wanted to be a symbol

00:00:07.947 --> 00:00:10.021
of inspiration, of possibilities.

00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:11.680
You if you want to build something

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.661
really powerful and really big,

00:00:12.661 --> 00:00:14.247
and expand and grow, you've got to

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.118
learn to be able to work with a team.

00:00:16.118 --> 00:00:20.391
- You're like really good
at leading, it's crazy.

00:00:20.391 --> 00:00:22.262
- I'm a New York Times
best selling author.

00:00:22.262 --> 00:00:24.989
I'm a top 100 podcaster in the world.

00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:27.316
I'm a former professional football player.

00:00:27.316 --> 00:00:28.751
I used to hold a world record for

00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:31.248
the most receiving yards in a single game.

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:33.808
I'm an entrepreneur, I'm
a coach, I'm a speaker.

00:00:33.808 --> 00:00:35.428
My name is Lewis Howes and this is my

00:00:35.428 --> 00:00:38.292
Top Ten Rules for Success.

00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:40.133
- Rule number three is
my personal favorite.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.759
And I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:42.759 --> 00:00:44.152
And as always, as you're listening,

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:46.166
if something really resonates with you,

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:48.196
there's a message that
really holds true to you,

00:00:48.196 --> 00:00:50.042
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:50.042 --> 00:00:53.104
and put it in quotes, so that
other people can be inspired.

00:00:53.104 --> 00:00:54.581
And when you write it down, it's much

00:00:54.581 --> 00:00:58.748
more likely to stick with
yourself as well, enjoy.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:04.110
(upbeat music)

00:01:11.382 --> 00:01:13.120
- I think you got to have a dream first.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.054
You know, for me it always
starts with a dream.

00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:18.723
Because I can go through any adversity

00:01:18.723 --> 00:01:20.738
when I have a dream, something
I'm passionate about.

00:01:20.738 --> 00:01:22.976
When I'm not excited about something,

00:01:22.976 --> 00:01:25.847
then I want to give up
or I don't want to do it.

00:01:25.847 --> 00:01:27.383
I want to go back to
thinking about my dream.

00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:28.643
And so I think first,
we have to figure out

00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:30.035
what is our dream?

00:01:30.035 --> 00:01:32.609
And go on a journey and
a path to achieving that.

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:35.612
And, you know, years ago I was telling

00:01:35.612 --> 00:01:38.223
Scooter, our mutual friend,
backstage years ago,

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:39.756
when I didn't have much,
I remember watching

00:01:39.756 --> 00:01:41.461
this show and seeing people dance.

00:01:41.461 --> 00:01:43.268
And I literally envisioned in my head

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:46.309
hip bumping you, dancing on this stage.

00:01:46.309 --> 00:01:47.272
- And we did it.

00:01:47.272 --> 00:01:48.105
- We did it.

00:01:48.105 --> 00:01:48.938
- Wow!

00:01:48.938 --> 00:01:52.192
(audience applauds)

00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:55.094
Listen, there are many
examples of that kind

00:01:55.094 --> 00:01:58.413
of believing it and achieving it.

00:01:58.413 --> 00:01:59.908
- The first one that
most people come to me

00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:02.768
is they don't have a clear
vision of what they want.

00:02:02.768 --> 00:02:03.847
They want a better life.

00:02:03.847 --> 00:02:04.809
They want to make more money.

00:02:04.809 --> 00:02:07.123
They want to have a better
relationship but they're not clear.

00:02:07.123 --> 00:02:09.111
And the greatest minds,
and the greatest achievers

00:02:09.111 --> 00:02:12.167
are very specific and
clear on their vision.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.990
It's so certain to them what it is.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.627
They can see it, they can
feel it, they can taste it.

00:02:16.627 --> 00:02:18.275
And as an athlete I used to visualize

00:02:18.275 --> 00:02:20.942
how I wanted to create my sport.

00:02:21.978 --> 00:02:24.423
How I wanted to create myself in sports.

00:02:24.423 --> 00:02:27.284
And vision was very
powerful for me, back then,

00:02:27.284 --> 00:02:28.653
as it is now for the business world.

00:02:28.653 --> 00:02:30.509
So the first thing is vision, that people

00:02:30.509 --> 00:02:31.795
are going to get clear on.

00:02:31.795 --> 00:02:33.082
Started with vision.

00:02:33.082 --> 00:02:36.125
In sports we always start each season

00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:38.569
with a clear vision on the
chalk board in the locker room.

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:41.078
What are we looking to
achieve this season?

00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:42.716
Do we want to make the playoffs?

00:02:42.716 --> 00:02:44.119
Do we want to win the championship?

00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:45.482
We are always very clear.

00:02:45.482 --> 00:02:46.957
It's written up on the board.

00:02:46.957 --> 00:02:49.296
Every day we walk in the
locker room we see our vision.

00:02:49.296 --> 00:02:51.140
We know what we're working towards.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.171
So for me, I have a board with my vision.

00:02:54.171 --> 00:02:55.718
And every day I look at it.

00:02:55.718 --> 00:02:56.990
And I'm very clear and specific

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.333
about what it is and when
it's going to happen,

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.721
each six months to a year.

00:03:00.721 --> 00:03:02.348
Each season of my life.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.891
So I just try and translate all that

00:03:03.891 --> 00:03:05.128
I learned as an athlete, because that's

00:03:05.128 --> 00:03:06.962
all I knew, into life.

00:03:06.962 --> 00:03:08.610
And it's helped me get to, at least,

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.588
where I'm at currently.

00:03:10.588 --> 00:03:11.954
I lot of people, when they're trying

00:03:11.954 --> 00:03:13.630
to get success as an entrepreneur,

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.086
and they fail, it's because they

00:03:15.086 --> 00:03:17.919
don't first believe in themselves.

00:03:18.855 --> 00:03:21.418
Now, you've got to believe in yourself.

00:03:21.418 --> 00:03:23.380
You've got to build some
confidence in yourself.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.527
So that you can build
the right relationships.

00:03:25.527 --> 00:03:27.436
So that you can take action,
create the right products,

00:03:27.436 --> 00:03:30.400
deliver the service, sell yourself.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.440
Really, it's all about selling yourself

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.404
if you want to sell your
products and services.

00:03:34.404 --> 00:03:36.616
So you got to build some small wins.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:40.124
Little wins every single day,
to build that confidence.

00:03:40.124 --> 00:03:42.736
And start believing in yourself.

00:03:42.736 --> 00:03:45.686
- There's a lot of people
who get frustrated.

00:03:45.686 --> 00:03:47.494
Who then say, "You know, enough is enough.

00:03:47.494 --> 00:03:49.551
"I'm going to do something."

00:03:49.551 --> 00:03:51.603
and the next day they wake up and it's,

00:03:51.603 --> 00:03:52.800
they're like back to their old life.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.436
Like, they had this moment of boldness,

00:03:54.436 --> 00:03:56.606
moment of greatness, and then fall back

00:03:56.606 --> 00:03:58.414
into repeated patterns and habits,

00:03:58.414 --> 00:04:01.014
and life just gets them down again

00:04:01.014 --> 00:04:03.029
and they go back to their
job at their regular life.

00:04:03.029 --> 00:04:04.734
Like, how did you break that cycle?

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:06.489
And, "This is actually
the day I'm going to

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:09.285
"go and do something bigger."

00:04:09.285 --> 00:04:11.843
- I think it was just a moment
of, like, enough is enough.

00:04:11.843 --> 00:04:13.332
Like I was sleeping on my sister's couch

00:04:13.332 --> 00:04:16.165
for a couple of years, originally.

00:04:17.061 --> 00:04:18.701
And she had told me, "You know,

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:19.924
"are you going to start paying rent?"

00:04:19.924 --> 00:04:21.535
At about a year and 1/2 mark.

00:04:21.535 --> 00:04:22.380
(he laughs)

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.591
Like, "When are you going
to start paying rent?"

00:04:23.591 --> 00:04:24.878
Because I was just
eating her food for free.

00:04:24.878 --> 00:04:27.606
I was, a slob, I didn't clean up.

00:04:27.606 --> 00:04:30.831
I was just taking
advantage of the situation.

00:04:30.831 --> 00:04:32.119
And I was 24 years old or something.

00:04:32.119 --> 00:04:34.405
And I remember just being, "It's time

00:04:34.405 --> 00:04:36.877
"for me to grow up and do
something with my life."

00:04:36.877 --> 00:04:40.061
I've sat here for a year and
1/2 almost two years now.

00:04:40.061 --> 00:04:44.228
Depressed, miserable, whatever
I was doing, Making excuses.

00:04:45.649 --> 00:04:46.834
"This isn't who I want to be.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.291
"I aspire to be something greater.

00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:53.294
"My parents didn't raise
me to be this way."

00:04:53.294 --> 00:04:55.009
I wanted to make myself proud.

00:04:55.009 --> 00:04:56.646
I wanted to make my last name proud.

00:04:56.646 --> 00:04:59.328
I wanted to make my family proud.

00:04:59.328 --> 00:05:01.226
And I wanted to be a symbol.

00:05:01.226 --> 00:05:05.138
I think I've always wanted to be a symbol

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.583
of inspiration, of possibilities.

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:10.700
From my sports days,
I remember the feeling

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.783
after the games when parents or fans,

00:05:15.941 --> 00:05:18.839
or parents of other
players from other teams,

00:05:18.839 --> 00:05:21.480
would come up to me and say, "Thank you

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.192
"for showing me what's possible.

00:05:23.192 --> 00:05:25.978
"There was no way you were going to

00:05:25.978 --> 00:05:28.083
"be able to catch that ball,
but somehow you did that.

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:29.657
"It blew my mind.

00:05:29.657 --> 00:05:30.619
"There's no way you guys should have

00:05:30.619 --> 00:05:32.996
"come back after how much you were down.

00:05:32.996 --> 00:05:34.936
"And what you did blew me away."

00:05:34.936 --> 00:05:37.285
I loved hearing that.

00:05:37.285 --> 00:05:41.097
And seeing in other people,
the spark of passion,

00:05:41.097 --> 00:05:43.320
excitement, of possibility, for what

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.489
they could create in their life.

00:05:45.489 --> 00:05:49.689
And I wanted to be that symbol of passion,

00:05:49.689 --> 00:05:51.792
and vision, and focus, and commitment

00:05:51.792 --> 00:05:56.119
towards my dream, to show
others what's possible.

00:05:56.119 --> 00:05:58.466
And I've never been the
best at anything I've done.

00:05:58.466 --> 00:06:01.974
You know, in sports I
was always the underdog.

00:06:01.974 --> 00:06:06.141
I was never the biggest,
fastest, or strongest dog.

00:06:07.084 --> 00:06:10.457
And I think I just wanted
to show it's possible.

00:06:10.457 --> 00:06:11.646
So that's what I'm still doing.

00:06:11.646 --> 00:06:12.608
It's like, I'm just a kid from

00:06:12.608 --> 00:06:14.428
a small town of Delaware, Ohio.

00:06:14.428 --> 00:06:18.595
Who had a lot of emotional
turmoil inside, growing up.

00:06:19.887 --> 00:06:23.905
And I'm trying to show
people what's possible.

00:06:23.905 --> 00:06:25.335
No matter where you come from.

00:06:25.335 --> 00:06:26.195
I built it up.

00:06:26.195 --> 00:06:27.060
I didn't have that big of an audience

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.833
when I started, almost three years ago.

00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:30.093
I had a pretty decent size, but I had

00:06:30.093 --> 00:06:31.938
the relationships with influencers,

00:06:31.938 --> 00:06:35.228
from the years of previous
stuff with my other business.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.035
So I was able to get a
lot of great influencers

00:06:37.035 --> 00:06:40.001
on because I'd do an interview podcast.

00:06:40.001 --> 00:06:42.718
And I was just consistent, I said,

00:06:42.718 --> 00:06:45.148
"I'm going to do it every
week, for this year."

00:06:45.148 --> 00:06:46.280
And I'd do one once a week.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:47.163
Then the second year I said, "I'm going to

00:06:47.163 --> 00:06:48.695
"do it twice a week, this year."

00:06:48.695 --> 00:06:50.438
Because people were asking for more.

00:06:50.438 --> 00:06:52.584
Then the third year, now, people said,

00:06:52.584 --> 00:06:53.468
"We want more."

00:06:53.468 --> 00:06:55.184
So I said, "I'm going to
do it three times a week."

00:06:55.184 --> 00:06:57.849
And so, I'm at 240
episodes, almost, right now,

00:06:57.849 --> 00:06:59.736
over a three year period.

00:06:59.736 --> 00:07:02.373
And I still feel like I'm
scratching the surface.

00:07:02.373 --> 00:07:04.139
But I'm almost three years in,

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:06.441
at the end of three years
and I still love it.

00:07:06.441 --> 00:07:07.454
So I think a lot of people get into

00:07:07.454 --> 00:07:09.078
a podcast because they feel they need

00:07:09.078 --> 00:07:10.614
to do it, or they want to do it.

00:07:10.614 --> 00:07:11.682
And they'll talk about a topic

00:07:11.682 --> 00:07:13.912
for six months and then they're burnt out.

00:07:13.912 --> 00:07:15.214
So I think if you're
going to do a podcast,

00:07:15.214 --> 00:07:16.945
do something that you're committed to

00:07:16.945 --> 00:07:19.247
for the next three, five, 10 years.

00:07:19.247 --> 00:07:22.028
If you really want to see
it grow and build momentum

00:07:22.028 --> 00:07:25.096
around your brand and have an impact.

00:07:25.096 --> 00:07:28.114
We always had this goal in sport.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:30.272
And I give the credit to my coaches

00:07:30.272 --> 00:07:31.702
for instilling that in me.

00:07:31.702 --> 00:07:33.340
He was like, always creating this goal,

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.574
this par time to achieve something.

00:07:36.574 --> 00:07:38.668
And during that time,
nothing else mattered.

00:07:38.668 --> 00:07:42.293
It didn't matter what was
happening in school, for me.

00:07:42.293 --> 00:07:43.173
Relationships didn't matter.

00:07:43.173 --> 00:07:44.969
It was just, achieving that goal.

00:07:44.969 --> 00:07:47.882
And maybe it comes back
to childhood or something,

00:07:47.882 --> 00:07:49.780
where I just wanted to be a great athlete.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.704
But when I get in that
mind frame, I guess.

00:07:52.704 --> 00:07:54.383
I don't know, I just want to achieve

00:07:54.383 --> 00:07:56.451
the goal more than anything else.

00:07:56.451 --> 00:07:58.715
And that's what I like to do.

00:07:58.715 --> 00:08:01.338
Learning to be with a team,
learning to be coachable.

00:08:01.338 --> 00:08:04.677
I wasn't the best athlete
but I was very coachable.

00:08:04.677 --> 00:08:06.692
So once I learned that, "Okay, how am I

00:08:06.692 --> 00:08:07.537
"going to build a business.

00:08:07.537 --> 00:08:09.854
"How am I going to do
anything outside of sports.

00:08:09.854 --> 00:08:11.178
"Well the first thing I need is a coach."

00:08:11.178 --> 00:08:13.706
Because that's the only way
I was successful in sports.

00:08:13.706 --> 00:08:16.483
So I hired coaches and mentors early on.

00:08:16.483 --> 00:08:18.743
And I just know that the greatest

00:08:18.743 --> 00:08:21.396
athletes in the world, can
never do it on their own.

00:08:21.396 --> 00:08:22.878
They always have a coach, even when

00:08:22.878 --> 00:08:26.142
they're at their peak,
they hire better coaches.

00:08:26.142 --> 00:08:27.573
So for me, coaches, and then learning

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.274
how to work with a team.

00:08:29.274 --> 00:08:30.614
Can't achieve anything on your own.

00:08:30.614 --> 00:08:32.316
Can't achieve anything great, on your own.

00:08:32.316 --> 00:08:34.941
So I learned quickly about developing

00:08:34.941 --> 00:08:36.971
a team around me, of people much smarter,

00:08:36.971 --> 00:08:39.349
who could support my vision.

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:40.870
Building a powerful team.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.092
I think there's a lot of people,

00:08:42.092 --> 00:08:43.742
especially in the entrepreneurial world,

00:08:43.742 --> 00:08:45.069
they want to be a lone wolf, they want to

00:08:45.069 --> 00:08:47.590
do it on their own, no
one can do it like them,

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.216
no one's as good as them, no one knows

00:08:49.216 --> 00:08:50.790
how to do it like them.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.608
And that can only take you so far.

00:08:52.608 --> 00:08:54.197
So if you want to build
something really powerful,

00:08:54.197 --> 00:08:56.042
and really big, and expand, and grow,

00:08:56.042 --> 00:08:59.034
you've got to learn to be
able to work with a team.

00:08:59.034 --> 00:09:02.377
And you've got to lead
with some inspiration.

00:09:02.377 --> 00:09:04.418
You can't put people down
and make people feel bad,

00:09:04.418 --> 00:09:06.301
because there's a lot of different options

00:09:06.301 --> 00:09:07.629
these days for people to leave

00:09:07.629 --> 00:09:09.042
and go do whatever they want.

00:09:09.042 --> 00:09:10.644
So how're you going to
build a powerful team?

00:09:10.644 --> 00:09:13.217
Loving deeper, you know, relationships,

00:09:13.217 --> 00:09:16.896
I've discovered, are the
key to success in life.

00:09:16.896 --> 00:09:20.405
And the key to successful
relationships are loving deeper,

00:09:20.405 --> 00:09:22.903
and being more vulnerable and intimate

00:09:22.903 --> 00:09:24.658
and showing yourself.

00:09:24.658 --> 00:09:26.216
And I think we've missed that sometimes.

00:09:26.216 --> 00:09:27.452
We're so busy, we're so focused on

00:09:27.452 --> 00:09:30.312
our own selves and our cell phones,

00:09:30.312 --> 00:09:31.586
whatever it may be.

00:09:31.586 --> 00:09:33.732
That we don't take time
to connect like this.

00:09:33.732 --> 00:09:35.174
And just look in someone's eyes

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:37.435
and tell them what their dream is,

00:09:37.435 --> 00:09:39.913
and how they feel, and listen.

00:09:39.913 --> 00:09:42.169
So relationships are the
key to success, in my mind.

00:09:42.169 --> 00:09:44.968
I just went to India to get certified

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:47.053
to be a meditation instructor.

00:09:47.053 --> 00:09:49.167
Went through a two week process.

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:52.949
And it's something I try
to do on a daily basis.

00:09:52.949 --> 00:09:56.968
And when I implement a daily
meditation practice, I feel it.

00:09:56.968 --> 00:09:59.865
I feel positive, I feel clear,

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:03.783
I feel intentional about what
I'm doing, I'm less reactive.

00:10:03.783 --> 00:10:05.124
Since I've been back, there's been days

00:10:05.124 --> 00:10:07.269
I've missed doing my meditation.

00:10:07.269 --> 00:10:09.971
And since missing them, I feel lethargic.

00:10:09.971 --> 00:10:13.193
I feel lazier, I feel more reactive

00:10:13.193 --> 00:10:15.111
or frustrated in certain times.

00:10:15.111 --> 00:10:17.221
So I definitely feel the difference

00:10:17.221 --> 00:10:20.109
the days I meditate
versus the days I don't.

